{%- doc -%}
  Keeps exactly one visible language/currency switcher.

  The theme's own localization-form (rendered in the header dropdown and the
  mobile drawer) already routes correctly to every published locale and to
  real Shopify Markets currencies — verified live. The Transtore app injects
  a second, independent switcher plus an auto-opening geolocation popup on
  every page. Rather than showing both, this hides Transtore's front-end UI
  so only the theme's native switcher is visible. Transtore itself stays
  installed; nothing here touches the app or its settings — this only
  affects what renders on the storefront.

  Reported symptom this is also aimed at: visitors on Android/iPhone/tablet
  saw scrolling stop intermittently. Transtore's geo popup locks page scroll
  by toggling a class on <html> while it is "open" — with the popup hidden
  via CSS, that class can still get added (and, on a slow connection, added
  before this file's own stylesheet has loaded) without ever being cleared,
  stranding the page unscrollable. The stylesheet override handles the
  normal case; the script below is a belt-and-suspenders fix that actively
  strips the class the moment it appears, so a cascade/timing loss never
  leaves a real visitor stuck.

  @example
  {% render 'irth-single-switcher' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .ts-switcher-individual,
  .ts-geo {
    display: none !important;
  }

  /* The geo popup sets a class on <html> that locks page scroll while open.
     With the popup hidden, that lock would otherwise strand the page
     unscrollable, so it is released here. */
  html.ts-geo-opened {
    overflow: auto !important;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

<script>
  (function () {
    var html = document.documentElement;

    var clearLock = function () {
      if (html.classList.contains('ts-geo-opened')) {
        html.classList.remove('ts-geo-opened');
      }
    };

    clearLock();

    new MutationObserver(clearLock).observe(html, {
      attributes: true,
      attributeFilter: ['class'],
    });
  })();
</script>
